}

^["lab_format"]{
 # Format is owned by ../curriculum-html-css-mastery/wip.spw (see its lab_format frame). This frame records only what is svg-specific.
 ~#home: "docs/learn/labs/html-svg/, created by this plan only after html-css commit 1 lands the shared home, README and runner"
 ~#tiers_here: "structural (viewBox, attributes, element tree via jsdom), pure (path data parsed and evaluated in TypeScript), browser (rendering, filters, SMIL timing; attested by hand)"
 ~#known_gap: "jsdom lacks getTotalLength and getBBox on path elements, so geometry claims need the pure tier"
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-02-20 02:32] observe — SVG is often treated as a black box (exported assets) rather than a hand-coded, deeply integrated extension of the DOM.
 >>[2026-02-20 02:32] decide — This curriculum will focus on raw, hand-authored SVG specs (coordinate math, path calculus, filter composition) and how they reflect Spw's rendering paradigms (lenses, shaders, stages).
 >>[2026-02-20 05:45] revise — Expanded plan to 50 commits to match the rigor of html-css-mastery, breaking the curriculum into 5 deep-dive phases of 10 commits each.
 >>[2026-03-28 09:47] implement — added references/index.spw and richer development frames so SVG coordinates, paths, filters, animation, and foreignObject interop become topical anchors with reusable heuristics instead of diffuse reading memory.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:25] revise — Collapsed 50 lesson-stub commits to 7 work units (hygiene preflight, five labs-svg files, one snippet fold-in); no labs-svg directory exists in git history. Lesson list kept as ~#covers. Replaced two template wonders with a precedent audit of in-repo SVG.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:54] decide — reheat these curricula, 2026-10-12
 >>[2026-10-12 14:54] revise — Reheated to planning. Lab home docs/learn/labs/html-svg under the shared format owned by curriculum-html-css-mastery; needs edge added. Lab 1.01 is commit 1, blocked on the css home commit. jsdom lacks getTotalLength and getBBox, so path claims need a pure-tier evaluator.
}

^["open"]{
